---
import PrivacyControls from "../components/PrivacyControls.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy — Vraj Patel" description="What this site collects, why I use analytics and session replay, and how to opt out.">
  <header class="privacy-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Site / Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p>I use PostHog to understand how visitors use this site and spot problems. Analytics and session replay are on by default. You can opt out of either below.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="privacy-content">
    <PrivacyControls />

    <section aria-labelledby="analytics-heading">
      <h2 id="analytics-heading">Analytics</h2>
      <p>PostHog records which pages people visit, how long they stay, and how they interact with the site. This includes clicks, heatmaps, page-loading measurements, and dead clicks—clicks that produce no visible response.</p>
      <p>I don’t link this activity to your name or an account.</p>
      <p>The page you came from and campaign tags may be retained to show how visitors find the site. Query strings and fragments are removed from recorded page URLs. Advertising click IDs are discarded.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="replay-heading">
      <h2 id="replay-heading">Session replay</h2>
      <p>Session replay shows how a visit unfolds, which helps me find confusing interactions or broken controls. Text entered in form fields is masked in the replay.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="storage-heading">
      <h2 id="storage-heading">What this browser stores</h2>
      <p>Your privacy settings are saved in local storage. PostHog may also use first-party cookies or local storage to keep track of visits and when you leave a page.</p>
      <p>Your theme and shortcut preferences are saved separately and aren’t sent to PostHog.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="processor-heading">
      <h2 id="processor-heading">Hosting and data processing</h2>
      <p>GitHub Pages hosts this site. PostHog’s US Cloud service processes the analytics data and masked session replays.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
      <h2 id="contact-heading">Questions or concerns</h2>
      <p>For a privacy or security concern, <a href="https://github.com/basechildren/vrajmpatel.com/security/advisories/new">send a private report on GitHub</a>.</p>
      <p>For general questions, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/vrajmp/">contact me on LinkedIn</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-header, .privacy-content { max-width: 44rem; margin-inline: auto; }
  .privacy-header { padding-bottom: 2.25rem; }
  .privacy-header > p:last-child { margin-top: 1.25rem; max-width: 58ch; color: var(--copy); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.85; }
  .privacy-content { display: grid; gap: 2.75rem; }
  .privacy-content h2 { color: var(--ink); font-size: 1.375rem; line-height: 1.3; font-weight: 550; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .privacy-content p { margin-top: .9rem; color: var(--copy); font-size: .9375rem; line-height: 1.85; }
  .privacy-content a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--line); text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .privacy-content a:hover { color: var(--accent); text-decoration-color: currentColor; }
</style>
